  "chapter": 414,
  "signer": "ANDREW M. CUOMO",
  "text": "\n \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 19 Chapter 414\n \n       MEMORANDUM filed with Assembly Bill Number 5677, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT to amend the insurance law, in relation to health insurance\n        coverage for mammography by breast tomosynthesis\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  Breast tomosynthesis, or 3-D mammography, is a  lifesaving  technology\nthat  can  facilitate the early detection of breast cancer. Coverage for\nbreast tomosynthesis is required under existing Insurance  Law  mandates\nfor  mammography  screening when medically necessary. Earlier this year,\nthe Department of Financial Services issued Supplement No. 1  to  Insur-\nance  Circular  Letter  No. 2 (2016) discussing the coverage mandate for\nbreast tomosynthesis, and requesting that insurers use the  most  up-to-\ndate  clinical  review criteria when determining whether breast tomosyn-\nthesis is medically necessary.\n \n  Consistent with the Department's Circular  Letters,  this  bill  would\ncodify  the requirement that health insurers cover breast tomosynthesis.\nImportantly, however, it does not  eliminate  an  insurer's  ability  to\nreview breast tomosynthesis for medical necessity. The ability to review\nfor  medical  necessity is critical, as providing coverage for medically\nunnecessary care results in increased costs for the State and consumers.\nThis bill strikes a proper balance between a patient's ability to obtain\ncoverage for breast tomosynthesis and an insurer's ability to review the\nuse of the screening procedure for medical necessity. On that  basis,  I\nam signing this bill.\n \n  This bill is approved.                      (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n \n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2017
 },
